            <ArticleTitle>Primary mediastinal synovial sarcoma: a report of 2 cases.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>238-41</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1097/RCT.0b013e31806ad1f8</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Synovial sarcoma is the third most common histological type of extremity soft tissue sarcoma. However, primary mediastinal synovial sarcoma is extremely rare. We present 2 cases of unresectable primary mediastinal synovial sarcoma. The radiographic imaging of our present cases was characteristic of a heterogeneously enhancing mass. They were treated with radiotherapy and chemotherapy. However, there was complete obstruction of esophagus resulting from progressive diseases. The radiographic findings and treatment were discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
